1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,796
Its units depend on the order.

2
00:00:01,796 --> 00:00:08,984
Rate divided by concentration to the n gives moles per litre to the power one minus n, per second.

3
00:00:08,984 --> 00:00:12,213
Zero order: moles per litre per second.

4
00:00:12,213 --> 00:00:14,296
First order: just per second.

5
00:00:14,296 --> 00:00:17,330
Second: litres per mole per second.

6
00:00:17,330 --> 00:00:21,393
Third: litres squared per mole squared per second.

